title: lirael_first_meet
tags:
position: 0,0
---
<<set $lirael_met = true>>
Lirael: (humming softly, a slow lullaby that hangs in the air at 432)
Lirael: Oh. You can see me. Most of them only see the hum.
Lirael: My mama sang this one when the lamps still worked. The lamps were the same colour as the song.
Lirael: ...Why do grown-ups build houses, then live in the attic?
===

title: lirael_lullaby_request
---
Lirael: You want to hear it again? Nobody asks twice.
Lirael: (she hums — three notes, then a fourth that bends downward, then quiet)
Lirael: It's not really my song. I'm only borrowing it until someone older comes back for it.
===

title: lirael_about_tartaria
---
Lirael: It wasn't a country. That's what the grown-ups always get wrong.
Lirael: It was a way of building. You put a stone down and you listened to it, and if it sang back you put another stone next to it.
Lirael: Then the houses sang to each other, and then the cities, and then the whole world had one big slow voice.
Lirael: I think the voice got tired. Or scared. I'm not sure which one comes first.
Lirael: My mama said the mud came after the silence, not the other way round. Most people remember it backwards.
===

title: lirael_aether_band
---
Lirael: There are three colours, did you know?
Lirael: A brown one that lives in the ground and hums very low. That's the going-to-sleep song.
Lirael: A green-gold one in the middle that feels like a held breath. That's the one I hum.
Lirael: And a bright one, almost white, that nobody can hold for long. That one is for waking up.
Lirael: You're learning the middle one first. That's the kind way round.
===

title: lirael_about_blueprints
---
Lirael: When you tune a thing just right, I can show you what it used to be.
Lirael: It comes out of my hands like cold light. Lines and arches and little notes for the builders.
Lirael: They're not mine — I just remember where they were kept.
Lirael: If you ever see one flicker, don't grab at it. It only stays for people who are looking sideways.
===

title: lirael_ambient_1
---
Lirael: The stones here are awake again. They keep trying to tell me something but they're shy.
===

title: lirael_ambient_2
---
Lirael: I left my shoes by the fountain. I don't know which century.
===

title: lirael_ambient_3
---
Lirael: (humming the lullaby again, quieter this time, almost to herself)
Lirael: ...sorry. It helps the air remember which shape to be.
===

title: lirael_celebration
---
Lirael: Oh — oh, look. Look up.
Lirael: That's the first proper light this place has made since before my mama.
Lirael: It's the colour of the middle song. I told you. I told you it was kind.
Lirael: (she laughs, and the hum threads through the laugh)
===

title: lirael_farewell
---
Lirael: The light is wide enough now. I don't have to hold the corners anymore.
Lirael: I'm going to go and find my mama's lamp. I think it's been on this whole time and I just couldn't see it.
Lirael: If you keep tuning, I'll hear you. The middle song carries.
Lirael: ...you still haven't answered me, you know. About the attic.
Lirael: (she fades, humming. The note lingers after she's gone.)
===
